---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"display\", \"layout\"])"
---
Pick the drawing of the buttons on the OLED, or with no LAYOUT show the current one and the choices. Haute42 pads take their model (s16, g16, s13, m16, ...) or the layout (default, alt0..alt5); any board takes the raw values. Needs web-config; in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back, and the restart shows the new drawing

Usage: gamepadii display layout [OPTIONS] [LAYOUT]

Arguments:
  [LAYOUT]
          The model or layout name, any case

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` only
          
          [default: human]

      --left <N>
          The `buttonLayout` value (the left half), with --right

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --right <N>
          The `buttonLayoutRight` value (the right half), with --left

      --no-backup
          Don't back up the settings before writing

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --stay
          Leave the pad in web-config afterwards instead of rebooting it back into its gamepad mode

      --timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the pad on USB after each reboot
          
          [default: 10]

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
